d in Mosul, in the Nineveh Governorate of Iraq. It is situated in the Taqafah district, bordering the Tigris river near the Nineveh archeological site. When completed, it will be the largest mosque in Mosul.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Mosul Grand Mosque","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Grand_mosque_of_Mosul_.jpg/1280px-Grand_mosque_of_Mosul_.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Grand_mosque_of_Mosul_.jpg/500px-Grand_mosque_of_Mosul_.jpg","w":1200,"h":636,"author":"Omar Siddeeq Yousif","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_mosque_of_Mosul_.jpg"}},{"id":"mosul_al_mujahidi_mosque","areaId":"mosul","name":"Al-Mujahidi Mosque","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":36.34016,"lng":43.14054},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"mosul_al_mujahidi_mosque","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":15,"commonsNearby":21,"wikiPageviews":35,"wikidataSitelinks":7,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["almujahidimosque","mosul"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Al-Mujahidi Mosque is a historic mosque located in Mosul, Iraq. The mosque dates back to the 12th century and witnessed many renovations since then. The mosque was also known for having many names each based on its own story.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Al-Mujahidi Mosque","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/%D8%AC%D8%A7%D9%85%D8%B9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AE%D8%B6%D8%B1_%D9%81%D9%8A_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%88%D8%B5%D9%84.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/